# Import boundaries — history brought in from another repository.
#
# The Smart Commit convention (.githooks/lint-commits.sh) requires every
# non-merge commit to carry a UIFPE key and a #comment. History imported from
# another repository cannot satisfy that: those commits were authored before
# this convention existed, under another repository's rules, and rewriting them
# to add keys would destroy the history the import was performed to preserve.
#
# Each line below records the tip of one imported history. That commit and all
# of its ancestors are exempt from the convention. Everything authored in this
# repository is still linted — recording a boundary narrows the exemption to
# foreign history and nothing else.
#
# Format:  <full-or-short-sha>  <what was imported, and the PR that did it>
#
# Adding a line is a deliberate act. It must name the source repository and the
# pull request, so the exemption is auditable years later. If a SHA here is not
# present in the repository the linter warns and ignores it, so a stale line
# degrades to a no-op rather than silently widening the exemption.

